#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:5
#: f9ee83d553e54108b9b281cb7320eb5a
msgid "Maxbotix I2C Sonar Rangefinder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:7
#: 8790b5049758419084c30c9cece925db
msgid "`Maxbotix I2C EZ4 <https://www.maxbotix.com/product-category/i2cxl-maxsonar-ez-products>`__ sonar (also known as the I2CXL-MaxSonar-EZ4 or MB1242) is a relatively inexpensive, short range (up to 7m) range finder primarily designed for indoor use but which has been successfully used outdoors on Copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:12
#: 02e4b132bea74d81b5bf74d76c989375
msgid "The EZ4 (recommended) has the narrowest beam providing the best noise resistance while the EZ0 has the widest beam and highest sensitivity. `The datasheet can be found here <https://www.maxbotix.com/documents/I2CXL-MaxSonar-EZ_Datasheet.pdf>`__. Additional information on the similar :ref:`analog version of this sonar can be found here <copter:sonar>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:20
#: b295e3a6b48649c9b5f05db59560dc02
msgid "``RNGFNDx_MAX`` must be set to a tested, appropriate value.  If ``RNGFNDx_MAX`` is set to a value greater than the range of the sensor, the autopilot will not respond correctly to the data provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:25
#: f3d3b3d4153e42689e90ab47c6721f88
msgid "Connecting to the Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:27
#: c891985f843d43188257a3e588a2b5c4
msgid "The sonar should be connected to the Pixhawk's I2C port as shown below or alternatively through an I2C expansion board. The Pixhawk will provide the regulated 5V power supply the sensor requires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:35
#: fe78d77e14004cc1afa2c8485b20e35e
msgid "Setup through the mission planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:37
#: d154b00f00064116a491c0159aaf62b6
msgid "To configure Copter, Plane or Rover to use the Maxbotix I2C, please first connect with the Mission Planner and then open the Config/Tuning >> Full Parameter List page and set the following parameters (example below is if it is first rangefinder):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:41
#: 3036899811bf4fe2ba6fad6d07babed2
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MAX<RNGFND1_MAX>` = \"7\" (i.e. 7m max range)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:42
#: 5973de3318064284b51497cbc61cf930
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_TYPE<RNGFND1_TYPE>` = “2\" (MaxbotixI2C sonar)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:48
#: 6696a890c4204092ad2324ce179dfea2
msgid "Testing the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-maxbotixi2c.rst:50
#: a19b75ac41284bafa99ac920db03533c
msgid "Distances read by the sensor can be seen in the Mission Planner's Flight Data screen's Status tab. Look closely for \"rangefinder1\"."
msgstr ""
